cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or build on this design, please cite it as below."
title: "Yeah Hand (Rebelia V2): an open source tendon-driven robotic and prosthetic hand"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Lumare"
    given-names: "Vittorio"
    email: "vittorio.lumare@robotgarage.org"
abstract: >-
  Open source anthropomorphic hand, 3D-printable, for robots and prostheses.
  Five serial bus servomotors housed in the hand skeleton drive the fingers
  through antagonistic flexion and extension tendons guided by PTFE Bowden
  tubes and fixed to a two-part spool per actuator. The thumb rotation servo
  is mounted on a removable platform. The ESP32 firmware provides calibration,
  force-limited grasps, grasp presets, ROS mode with position, load,
  temperature and current feedback, and two-channel EMG control in the
  prosthetic version. Successor of Rebelia V1 (OSHWA IT000021).
repository-code: "https://github.com/opsobot/yeah-hand"
license: CERN-OHL-S-2.0
version: "1.2"
date-released: "2026-09-14"
keywords:
  - open source hardware
  - robotic hand
  - prosthetic hand
  - tendon-driven
  - Bowden cable
  - gripper
  - ROS
  - ESP32
